<section class="how">
    <h2>How to Calculate Stripe Transaction Fees</h2>
    <p>Processing transactions online involves fee structures designed to offset compliance, fraud risk, and network expenses. With standard Stripe US processing, the formula consists of a percentage rate plus a flat fee per charge.</p>
    <p>Using this calculator is simple: enter the dollar value of your invoice or sales receipt and select your typical transaction category. Our tool instantly determines the precise cut Stripe takes, your actual payout, and also works backward to specify the gross billing amount needed to clear your target net earnings.</p>
</section>

<section class="formula">
    <h2>The Stripe Fee Equations</h2>
    <p>To calculate what you will receive (Standard payout math):</p>
    <p><code>Net Payout = Charge Amount - (Charge Amount × Rate Percentage) - Fixed Fee</code></p>
    <p>For example, at 2.9% + $0.30 on a <strong>$100.00</strong> transaction, the fee is: <code>($100.00 × 0.029) + $0.30 = $3.20</code>. Your net payout is <strong>$96.80</strong>.</p>
    <p>To calculate what you must invoice (Reverse charge math):</p>
    <p><code>Gross Invoice = (Net Target + Fixed Fee) / (1 - Rate Percentage)</code></p>
    <p>For example, if you want to clear exactly <strong>$100.00</strong> after a 2.9% + $0.30 fee: <code>($100.00 + $0.30) / (1 - 0.029) = $103.30 / 0.971 = $106.39</code>. You must charge <strong>$106.39</strong>.</p>
</section>

