<section class="faq">
    <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    
    <h3>How do I avoid paying Stripe transaction fees?</h3>
    <p>While you cannot force Stripe to discount transaction charges on standard credit cards, merchants frequently adjust agreements or utilize custom item pricing to request that customers contribute equivalent Processing Fee overhead. Alternatively, selecting ACH Direct Debit transactions reduces processing rate charges to 0.8% per transaction, capped at a maximum of $5.00.</p>
    
    <h3>Are Stripe fees refunded when I issue client refunds?</h3>
    <p>No. Effective in recent fee policy terms, Stripe does not return credit card processing interchange fees when a payments merchant issues a refund. You retain responsibility for the original percentage and flat processing expenses, meaning the cost of returns is borne entirely by the merchant.</p>
    
    <h3>Does Stripe charge a regular monthly recurring fee?</h3>
    <p>No. Stripe utilizes a pay-as-you-go financial format and does not demand set monthly minimums, subscription fees, or initial setup charges. You are solely billed for transactions processed through your Stripe account.</p>

    <h3>What determines an international card processing charge?</h3>
    <p>Stripe applies a 1% additional fee on credit cards issued outside of the United States. Furthermore, if currency conversion is required, a standard 1% fee is applied to the transaction total.</p>
